By default, promise executions are not assigned `asyncId`s due to the relatively expensive nature of the `async`/`await` will not get correct execution and trigger ids for promise callback contexts by default.
```
import { executionAsyncId, triggerAsyncId } from 'node:async_hooks';

Promise.resolve(1729).then(() => {
  console.log(`eid ${executionAsyncId()} tid ${triggerAsyncId()}`);
});
