The `node:child_process` module provides the ability to spawn subprocesses in a manner that is similar, but not identical, to [`child_process.spawn()`](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/child_process.html#child_processspawncommand-args-options) function:
```
const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');
const ls = spawn('ls', ['-lh', '/usr']);

ls.stdout.on('data', (data) => {
