The `process.dlopen()` method allows dynamically loading shared objects. It is primarily used by `require()` to load C++ Addons, and should not be used directly, except in special cases. In other words, [`require()`](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/globals.html#require) should be preferred over `process.dlopen()` unless there are specific reasons such as custom dlopen flags or loading from ES modules.
