The `process.stderr` property returns a stream connected to `stderr` (fd `2`). It is a [`net.Socket`](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/net.html#class-netsocket) (which is a [Duplex](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/stream.html#duplex-and-transform-streams) stream) unless fd `2` refers to a file, in which case it is a [Writable](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/stream.html#writable-streams) stream.
`process.stderr` differs from other Node.js streams in important ways. See [note on process I/O](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/process.html#a-note-on-process-io) for more information.
####  `process.stderr.fd`
