```
const pathname = '/a/b/c';
const search = '?d=e';
const hash = '#fgh';
const myURL = new URL(`https://example.org${pathname}${search}${hash}`); copy
```

To get the constructed URL string, use the `href` property accessor:
```
console.log(myURL.href); copy
