A value being `instanceof` a native error class is not equivalent to `isNativeError()` returning `true` for that value. `isNativeError()` returns `true` for errors which come from a different `instanceof Error` returns `false` for these errors:
```
import { createContext, runInContext } from 'node:vm';
import { types } from 'node:util';

const context = createContext({});
const myError = runInContext('new Error()', context);
console.log(types.isNativeError(myError)); // true
console.log(myError instanceof Error); // falseconst { createContext, runInContext } = require('node:vm');
const { types } = require('node:util');

const context = createContext({});
const myError = runInContext('new Error()', context);
console.log(types.isNativeError(myError)); // true
console.log(myError instanceof Error); // falsecopy
