#### Using `AsyncResource` for a `Worker` thread pool 
The following example shows how to use the `AsyncResource` class to properly provide async tracking for a [`Worker`](https://nodejs.org/api/worker_threads.html#class-worker) pool. Other resource pools, such as database connection pools, can follow a similar model.
Assuming that the task is adding two numbers, using a file named `task_processor.js` with the following content:
```
import { parentPort } from 'node:worker_threads';
parentPort.on('message', (task) => {
  parentPort.postMessage(task.a + task.b);
});const { parentPort } = require('node:worker_threads');
