### Class: `Decipheriv`
Added in: v0.1.94
  * Extends: [<stream.Transform>](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html#class-streamtransform)


Instances of the `Decipheriv` class are used to decrypt data. The class can be used in one of two ways:
  * As a [stream](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html) that is both readable and writable, where plain encrypted data is written to produce unencrypted data on the readable side, or
  * Using the [`decipher.update()`](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#decipherupdatedata-inputencoding-outputencoding) and [`decipher.final()`](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#decipherfinaloutputencoding) methods to produce the unencrypted data.


The [`crypto.createDecipheriv()`](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatedecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options) method is used to create `Decipheriv` instances. `Decipheriv` objects are not to be created directly using the `new` keyword.
Example: Using `Decipheriv` objects as streams:
```
import { Buffer } from 'node:buffer';
