####  `x509.checkIssued(otherCert)`
Added in: v15.6.0
  * `otherCert` [<X509Certificate>](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#class-x509certificate)
  * Returns: 


Checks whether this certificate was potentially issued by the given `otherCert` by comparing the certificate metadata.
This is useful for pruning a list of possible issuer certificates which have been selected using a more rudimentary filtering routine, i.e. just based on subject and issuer names.
Finally, to verify that this certificate's signature was produced by a private key corresponding to `otherCert`'s public key use [`x509.verify(publicKey)`](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#x509verifypublickey) with `otherCert`'s public key represented as a [`KeyObject`](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#class-keyobject) like so
```
if (!x509.verify(otherCert.publicKey)) {
  throw new Error('otherCert did not issue x509');
} copy
```

