The `'uncaughtExceptionMonitor'` event is emitted before an `'uncaughtException'` event is emitted or a hook installed via [`process.setUncaughtExceptionCaptureCallback()`](https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#processsetuncaughtexceptioncapturecallbackfn) is called.
Installing an `'uncaughtExceptionMonitor'` listener does not change the behavior once an `'uncaughtException'` event is emitted. The process will still crash if no `'uncaughtException'` listener is installed.
```
import process from 'node:process';

process.on('uncaughtExceptionMonitor', (err, origin) => {
  MyMonitoringTool.logSync(err, origin);
});

// Intentionally cause an exception, but don't catch it.
nonexistentFunc();
// Still crashes Node.jsconst process = require('node:process');

process.on('uncaughtExceptionMonitor', (err, origin) => {
  MyMonitoringTool.logSync(err, origin);
