The `process.stderr` property returns a stream connected to `stderr` (fd `2`). It is a [`net.Socket`](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#class-netsocket) (which is a [Duplex](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html#duplex-and-transform-streams) stream) unless fd `2` refers to a file, in which case it is a [Writable](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html#writable-streams) stream.
