####  `new TextDecoder([encoding[, options]])`
  * `encoding` `encoding` that this `TextDecoder` instance supports. **Default:** `'utf-8'`.
  * `options`
    * `fatal` `true` if decoding failures are fatal. This option is not supported when ICU is disabled (see [Internationalization](https://nodejs.org/api/intl.html)). **Default:** `false`.
    * `ignoreBOM` `true`, the `TextDecoder` will include the byte order mark in the decoded result. When `false`, the byte order mark will be removed from the output. This option is only used when `encoding` is `'utf-8'`, `'utf-16be'`, or `'utf-16le'`. **Default:** `false`.


Creates a new `TextDecoder` instance. The `encoding` may specify one of the supported encodings or an alias.
The `TextDecoder` class is also available on the global object.
####  `textDecoder.decode([input[, options]])`
  * `input` `ArrayBuffer`, `DataView`, or `TypedArray` instance containing the encoded data.
  * `options`
    * `stream` `true` if additional chunks of data are expected. **Default:** `false`.
  * Returns: 


Decodes the `input` and returns a string. If `options.stream` is `true`, any incomplete byte sequences occurring at the end of the `input` are buffered internally and emitted after the next call to `textDecoder.decode()`.
If `textDecoder.fatal` is `true`, decoding errors that occur will result in a `TypeError` being thrown.
####  `textDecoder.encoding`
The encoding supported by the `TextDecoder` instance.
####  `textDecoder.fatal`
The value will be `true` if decoding errors result in a `TypeError` being thrown.
####  `textDecoder.ignoreBOM`
The value will be `true` if the decoding result will include the byte order mark.
