Awaits the `asyncFn` promise or, if `asyncFn` is a function, immediately calls the function and awaits the returned promise to complete. It will then check that the promise is not rejected.
If `asyncFn` is a function and it throws an error synchronously, `assert.doesNotReject()` will return a rejected `Promise` with that error. If the function does not return a promise, `assert.doesNotReject()` will return a rejected `Promise` with an [`ERR_INVALID_RETURN_VALUE`](https://nodejs.org/api/errors.html#err_invalid_return_value) error. In both cases the error handler is skipped.
