####  `server.close([callback])`
History Version | Changes  
---|---  
v19.0.0 | The method closes idle connections before returning.  
v0.1.90 | Added in: v0.1.90  
  * `callback`


Stops the server from accepting new connections and closes all connections connected to this server which are not sending a request or waiting for a response. See [`net.Server.close()`](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#serverclosecallback).
```
const http = require('node:http');

const server = http.createServer({ keepAliveTimeout: 60000 }, (req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
  res.end(JSON.stringify({
    data: 'Hello World!',
  }));
});

