```

After response header was sent to the client, this property indicates the status message which was sent out.
####  `response.strictContentLength`
Added in: v18.10.0, v16.18.0
  * **Default:** `false`


If set to `true`, Node.js will check whether the `Content-Length` header value and the size of the body, in bytes, are equal. Mismatching the `Content-Length` header value will result in an `Error` being thrown, identified by `code:` [`'ERR_HTTP_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH'`](https://nodejs.org/api/errors.html#err_http_content_length_mismatch).
####  `response.uncork()`
Added in: v13.2.0, v12.16.0
See [`writable.uncork()`](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html#writableuncork).
####  `response.writableEnded`
Added in: v12.9.0
Is `true` after [`response.end()`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#responseenddata-encoding-callback) has been called. This property does not indicate whether the data has been flushed, for this use [`response.writableFinished`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#responsewritablefinished) instead.
####  `response.writableFinished`
Added in: v12.7.0
