The enabled module compile cache can be disabled by the [`NODE_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1`](https://nodejs.org/api/cli.html#node_disable_compile_cache1) environment variable. This can be useful when the compile cache leads to unexpected or undesired behaviors (e.g. less precise test coverage).
