Added in: v18.0.0, v16.17.0
  * `shouldRunOnlyTests` `only` tests.


If `shouldRunOnlyTests` is truthy, the test context will only run tests that have the `only` option set. Otherwise, all tests are run. If Node.js was not started with the [`--test-only`](https://nodejs.org/api/cli.html#--test-only) command-line option, this function is a no-op.
```
test('top level test', (t) => {
  // The test context can be set to run subtests with the 'only' option.
  t.runOnly(true);
  return Promise.all([
    t.test('this subtest is now skipped'),
    t.test('this subtest is run', { only: true }),
  ]);
}); copy
```

